## Why This Is Asked

Tests architectural judgment for cross-tenant data sharing, masking, governance, and external partner integration. Assesses telemetry discipline across async boundaries and how to promote configurations across environments.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-tenant export, data masking, consent-based sharing, audit trails
- Event-driven ingestion: Event Hubs, Functions; analytics/export: Synapse
- Telemetry propagation with OpenTelemetry across HTTP and downstream calls
- Security and config: App Configuration, Key Vault, Azure AD RBAC
- Testing: end-to-end traces, masking validation, failover scenarios

## Code Example

```javascript
// Node.js OpenTelemetry propagation in a function
const { trace, context, propagation } = require('@opentelemetry/api');
module.exports = async function (ctx, req) {
  const parent = propagation.extract(req.headers);
  const span = trace.getTracer('export').startSpan('export-per-tenant', undefined, parent);
  // downstream call
  span.end();
  ctx.log('export invoked');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate per-tenant masking rules across Salesforce and Snowflake exports?
- How would you test end-to-end traces across envs and during partial failures?

